The cross-PR batteries gain the three chain shapes end-to-end: the
defect's own (fma reads the inner negation, the outer survives for the
add -- nothing peels, bit-exact vs the reference compiler which also
materialises both links), the pinned-inner fold (one sign mask and a
vfnmadd reading the materialised inner), and the full-chain cancel to
the plain family. The ISA gate pins their asm exactly at both
-mno-avx2 spellings: chain_live keeps exactly two sign masks and takes
no sign latitude; chain_pin keeps one mask and folds to one vfnmadd;
shared_neg keeps zero masks and two vfnmsub. The shared-negation xorpd
pin was vacuous for every 4b target (\bxorpd\b can never match the VEX
spelling vxorpd -- no word boundary between v and x); it now matches
both spellings and the counts are re-verified by hand.

The batteries carry matched-arch .flags for the general suite's raw
oracle: they are contraction-sensitive by design (their sections pin
FMA family selection and the negation peel, and the default baseline
here contracts where the reference compiler's own default keeps the
libm call and double-rounds a*b+c), so the well-posed oracle is the
matched arch -- bit-exact raw, including NaN signs. The documented
C11 6.5p8 NaN-sign latitude is additionally canonicalised at print
time inside the batteries, for the consumers that compare across
baselines (the dedicated gate's SSE2 config). Input echoes and
promoted-table loads stay raw.

fma_isa_gate.c gains the two chain functions before shared_neg (the
per-function sed ranges stay disjoint) with the defect story in the
comments. The audit record gains defect 0 (the fixpoint direction,
the post-merge review's finding, adjudicated and extended with the
Signed-site closure), the git-verified test-count decomposition, and
the follow-up session's validation record.
